  nonce: '5968'  # 5968
  message: "F5 EMISSION-PARITY GATE FULLY CLOSED. Python class-attribute field slice merged dev 7752490cc4 (PR #4280) — the LAST strip. py.py now emits kind='field' for class-body Assign/AnnAssign (incl. dataclass fields x: int; instance attrs self.x excluded), class-scoped via assemble_stable_id. Self-analysis confirms it on hypergumbo's own substrate: ARCHITECTURE.md symbol count 33142 -> 35096 (+1954 class-field nodes), no baseline regressions. verify-generated had aged out (recorded SHA 89bd384770 fell out of the last-15 window after the session's slices) — recovered by regenerating ARCHITECTURE.md as a separate commit + AGit update push + merge-pr (NOT auto-pr, per the amend-orphan gotcha).\n\nThe emission-parity matrix (test_emission_parity_matrix.py) now has ZERO F5 holes: every emits_variable / emits_field cell is a hard lock. Eight per-language slices ratcheted the gate closed: JS/TS (fields + module vars, slices 1+2), Java (field + annotations), Go (struct field), C# (field + attributes), Rust (struct field + const/static, double strip), Swift (stored property + top-level let/var, double strip), Python (class attributes). 8 of the original strict-xfail holes were stripped; the 8 remaining matrix xfails are unrelated (java edge_imports INV-gojit + 7 entrypoint_concept WI-tosul).\n\nREMAINING WI-jusus scope (item stays todo_hard): the gate covers the 8 mainstream FIXTURE_ANALYZER languages. The long tail of OTHER analyzers (lang-common: kotlin/scala/dart/haskell/ocaml/...; lang-extended1: many) is not gated and may still not emit field/variable symbols — a future sweep, ideally gated by extending FIXTURE_ANALYZER. awaits_bakeoff_validation stays (all 8 slices are blast-radius emission changes pending DEEP cohort validation)."  # 5968
